---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — ruichenwei" description="Learn more about ruichenwei — background, interests, and what I'm working on.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-8">About Me</h1>

    <div class="prose max-w-none">
      <p>
        I'm someone who enjoys building things — tools, systems, and occasionally, websites like this one.
        My interests sit at the intersection of technology, productivity, and clear thinking.
      </p>

      <h2>What I'm Interested In</h2>
      <p>
        I spend most of my time thinking about how to use technology to work better, not just faster.
        This includes AI-assisted workflows, knowledge management systems, and developer tools that respect
        the user's time and attention.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm particularly drawn to tools that are simple, local-first, and built around plain text.
        I believe the best software gets out of your way and lets you focus on the work that matters.
      </p>

      <h2>How I Work</h2>
      <p>
        I build small, focused tools to solve problems I encounter in my own workflow. Rather than adopting
        large platforms, I prefer to understand the problem deeply and craft a minimal solution.
      </p>
      <p>
        My development philosophy centers on a few principles:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Start with the simplest thing that could work</li>
        <li>Prefer plain text and open formats</li>
        <li>Build for yourself first, then generalize if needed</li>
        <li>Write code that's easy to understand and modify</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Current Focus</h2>
      <p>
        Right now, I'm focused on:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Building and refining my personal productivity system</li>
        <li>Exploring how AI can assist with knowledge work without replacing judgment</li>
        <li>Writing about what I learn, both technical and non-technical</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Beyond Code</h2>
      <p>
        Outside of building things, I enjoy reading — mostly non-fiction on technology, design, and thinking.
        I believe that good ideas come from diverse inputs, so I try to read widely and outside my immediate field.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also think a lot about how we learn and how to build sustainable practices for growth.
        Learning in public — sharing what I'm figuring out, not just what I've mastered — is something I'm
        actively practicing.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in Touch</h2>
      <p>
        If any of this resonates with you, I'd be happy to connect. You can find me on
        <a href="https://github.com/Autoni09" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>,
        or reach out through my <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
